%S A399989 1,1,3,12,53,244,1146,5440,25981,124540,598366,2879248,13868466,
%T A399989 66846152,322353300,1555014848,7503120797,36209731180,174768906678,
%U A399989 843614321392,4072434343270,19660155199928,94915439717292,458247064630400,2212444181622578,10681996531477336
%N A399989 Number of fixed point free involutions in S_{2n} (or perfect matchings on [2n]) which avoid the permutations {123, 213, 231}.
%C A399989 As the following triples are shape Wilf equivalent, this sequence is also the number of perfect matchings on "2n" which avoid the pattern {123, 213, 312} or {132, 213, 231} or {132, 213, 312} or {32, 231, 321} or {132, 312, 321}.
%C A399989 Matchings that avoid patterns are as defined by Bloom and Elizalde.
%H A399989 Sucharita Biswas, Umesh Shankar and Sivaramakrishnan Sivasubramanian, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.08562">Matchings and shape-Wilf-Equivalence of sets of patterns of length three I: Triples</a>, arXiv:2609.08562 [math.CO], 2026. See Theorem 29.
%H A399989 Jonathan Bloom and Sergi Elizalde, <a href="https://doi.org/10.37236/2976">Pattern avoidance in matchings and partitions</a>, The Electronic Journal of Combinatorics, (2013) 20(2), #P5.
%F A399989 G.f.: (3*sqrt(1 - 4*x) - 1) / (2*sqrt(1 - 4*x) - 4*x).
%F A399989 A(x) satisfies (4*x^2+4*x-1)*A(x)^2 + (3-14*x)*A(x) + 9*x - 2 = 0 with a(0) = a(1) = 1.
%F A399989 For n >= 2, a(n) = 4*a(n-1) + 4*a(n-2) + A000108(n-1) - 6*A000108(n-2).
%Y A399989 Cf. A001147.
%K A399989 nonn
%O A399989 0,3
%A A399989 _Sivaramakrishnan Sivasubramanian_, Sep 18 2026
